cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DiracULA: Dirac Universal Language for Algorithm"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dmitriev
    given-names: Arkhip Alekseyevich
repository-code: "https://github.com/Arhip-Dmitriev/DiracULA"
url: "https://github.com/Arhip-Dmitriev/DiracULA"
abstract: >-
  A programming language for developing quantum algorithms without fixing the
  qudit count or dimension. Programs are written in Dirac notation and evaluated
  on symbolic path sums: states, Born distributions and post-measurement states
  are derived as closed forms that hold for every size, never by simulation.
  Results can be certified in Lean 4 and Mathlib by a verified normaliser of
  symbolic sums, and any state can be viewed as a qufinite ZXW diagram.
keywords:
  - dirac notation
  - quantum algorithms
  - quantum programming language
  - quantum computing
  - qudit
  - symbolic quantum
  - path sums
  - symbolic algebra
  - formal verification
  - lean
references:
  - type: software
    title: "ArchytasZX"
    authors:
      - family-names: Dmitriev
        given-names: Arkhip Alekseyevich
    url: "https://github.com/Arhip-Dmitriev/ArchytasZX"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
